0e05472767aa-a4f4-6c05-52045ce81fbe	Return exception if user is not found	2025-02-11 05:28:46+00	2025-02-11 05:29:24+00	0	<p>Referring to issue&nbsp;<a href="http://prom.projects4.me/app/project/aprom/issue/3520" data-tomark-pass="">#3520</a>, if the user has typed the incorrect username, the user shouldn't see the error message coming from the API different from the password message. The error message should be the same as when the user enters the wrong password. We shouldn't have to make clear to the end user in a more prominent way that "User is not found" or "Password is incorrect".</p>\n<p>That's why it should throw the same error in case of password and username mismatch.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3528	2025-02-12	2025-02-11	done	medium	cb4567905acd-06d6-1141-7dd99b59dd21	dbd06c04679c-02d0-dd6b-2dda26f8630c	\N	cbaa72735acd-06d6-1141-98f835ab32e9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	33f2e1c062c6-81f4-bcaf-6a1b411477d8	2025-02-11 05:40:47+00	AGAIA	0	0
0e6b556867f0-e0c3-c858-19a8f1b508f4	Add multi selection functionality in filter | List view	2025-04-04 16:34:22+00	2025-10-22 07:24:37+00	0	<p>There should be functionality where the user can set multiple values while filtering against a field e.g. status <strong>oneOf</strong>&nbsp;"in progress", "new" (for now we can select only one value from the dropdown).</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3599	2025-04-18	2025-04-04	in_progress	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	973277366887-2e85-fee8-668818bf5a45	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	f605b4e862c6-8e43-047e-0b80b37dd385	2025-10-21 13:51:20+00	APROM	0	1
0f49e3e7646d-4a23-a696-57a951c86d2e	Toggle the switch button of account status after updating the model	2023-05-24 07:13:19+00	2023-05-24 13:46:03+00	0	<p>Currently if we toggle multiple times on the mass switch button in order to change account statuses of multiple users then multiple XHR calls will go to our server.<br>\nLet say there were <strong>two</strong> calls sent to the server against <strong>USER 1</strong>. The change on the <i data-tomark-pass=""><strong>checked</strong></i>value on the switch button will be instantly shown to user but depending on the speed on the internet and how our server processes and send back the response, model will get updates&nbsp;<strong>two</strong>&nbsp;updates.<br>\nSo let say user gets response of 1st Patch call for <strong>USER 1</strong>&nbsp;after 2 sec and switch button is already set to is original set where it needs to be e.g <strong>ON</strong>, then after the 1st API call it will be turned to <strong>OFF</strong> and after 2nd API call it will turned to <strong>ON.</strong></p>\n<p>So the thing is we need to update the switch button toggle value after getting the APIs response.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3320	2023-05-24	2023-05-24	done	high	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	dbe1b8a1646b-d6c4-5d79-1ce28b13607e	\N	ae61a7235acb-1902-6b9c-e933ed4dfda0	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	23a4749162c6-89cf-bcaf-50ebb8c0446b	2023-05-24 13:46:03+00	APROM	0	0
