68ae177766d8-1b75-48f6-f188182bebd4	Error on Project detail view	2024-09-04 13:58:00+00	2024-09-05 05:35:47+00	0	<p><strong>Background:</strong><br>\nUsers encounter error on the project detail view.</p>\n<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong><br>\nThe project page should load without any error.</p>\n<p><strong>Steps to Reproduce:</strong><br>\n1. Go to application "/app" route.<br>\n2. Select one of the project from the project list.<br>\n3. The project detail view is loaded with an error.</p>\n<p><strong>Root Cause Analysis:</strong><br>\n<span class="colour" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51);" data-tomark-pass="">When a new user is created, a role named "Global role" is given to the user to assign initial default ACL permissions. So initially user is not part of any project and when they route to one of the projects, according to <strong>Prometheus</strong> code we render the list of Members. As the user is not a member of that project we get an error on fetching its role from the role lists in javascript.</span></p>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n<pre><code>runtime.js:5952 \n\nError occurred:\n\n- While rendering:\n  -top-level\n    application\n      app\n        app-layouts/application-wrapper\n          app.project\n            app.project.index\n              access-control\n</code></pre><pre><code>get-role.js:28 Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'get')\n    at getRole (get-role.js:28:1)\n    at index.js:3677:1\n    at SimpleClassicHelperManager.getValue (index.js:3681:1)\n    at manager.js:866:1\n    at reference.js:161:1\n    at track (validator.js:787:1)\n    at valueForRef (reference.js:160:1)\n    at Object.evaluate (runtime.js:3918:1)\n    at AppendOpcodes.evaluate (runtime.js:1284:1)\n    at LowLevelVM.evaluateSyscall (runtime.js:5064:1)\n</code></pre>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\n<br data-tomark-pass=""></p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bf