c9d61761673c-5261-d08b-7848567c0d4f	Add a new status lane in taskboard	2024-11-19 10:51:53+00	2025-11-18 07:35:37+00	0	<p>**Objective:**We need to add a new status lane called <strong>'In Review'</strong> to the taskboard in out frontend.&nbsp;This status will be used to track tasks that are in the review phase before they are marked as <strong>done</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Expected Behavior:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>'In Review'</strong> lane should be added between <strong>In Progress</strong> and <strong>Done</strong> on the taskboard.</li>\n<li>Tasks that are marked as "In Review" should be draggable between these lanes, just like other statuses.</li>\n<li>The task should display an appropriate label in the lane, and the drag-and-drop functionality should work without errors.</li>\n<li>Ensure that the UI aligns with the existing design patterns for consistency.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\n<strong>Implementation Details:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add the 'In Review' status to the static list of issue statuses e.g. <strong>statusesList</strong>&nbsp;in <strong>board.js</strong>.</li>\n<li>Modify the <strong>drag-and-drop functionality</strong> to support the new lane (ensure that the task can be moved to/from 'In Review').</li>\n<li>Ensure any relevant styles or visual updates are applied to the new status lane.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br data-tomark-pass=""><br>\n<strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>The 'In Review' lane is visible and draggable between <strong>In Progress</strong> and <strong>Done</strong>.</li>\n<li>Tasks can be moved into and out of the 'In Review' lane without errors.</li>\n<li>The taskboard UI updates properly without any visual inconsistencies.</li>\n<li>The taskboard remains functional after the new lane is added.</li>\n</ol>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	