bd5865735aef-38ce-5253-ce206e45d2b9	Use Ember Mirage	2018-05-06 21:12:29+00	2023-03-06 11:16:18+00	0	<p>When performing acceptance tests the build always fails.</p><p><br>This is because Prometheus expects actual data while there is no active API running on travis server.</p><p>User Ember Mirage to mock the API calls</p>	1	1	1	1	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3101	2018-05-06	2018-05-06	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	97d1fe826154-a785-3b25-81f3181d99d7	\N	ae5c14575acb-1902-6b9c-78da78712ee9	Hammad Hassan	Rana Nouman	\N	23a4749162c6-89cf-bcaf-50ebb8c0446b	\N	APROM	0	0
bdb6b1d465dc-1360-8ec3-95d85e71d137	Only update the permission flag which is updated, not all	2024-02-26 09:28:29+00	2024-02-26 10:01:44+00	0	<p>If we update only one flag of permission e.g. readF then according to our current solution it is updating all of the flags which is not a good solution.</p>\n<p>Let's say if the permission is not yet created on the first then all of its flags are set to "notset". When we set read flag's value to <strong>none</strong> and make a <strong>patch/post</strong> call, then the remaining flags also become part of the payload as empty values e.g. searchF:"" and the server returns 0 against these flags which makes all of the flags set to none, which is not desired.</p>\n	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	7ea8b586623c-5e99-bfcb-d51d01a7a16b	3395	2024-02-26	2024-02-26	done	medium	add12ff55acb-1902-6b9c-30d5411f7729	4e31873365d2-9931-48d2-91fe572f2988	\N	cb9597e45acd-06d6-1141-34137d85f7a9	Rana Nouman	Rana Nouman	\N	23a4749162c6-89cf-bcaf-50ebb8c0446b	2024-02-26 10:01:44+00	APROM	0	0
