d6694732583d-a500-dc60-5a3013ff6990	Overflow Scrolling	2016-11-29 05:08:38+00	2016-11-29 05:08:38+00	1	Hammad Hassan	1	Hammad Hassan	0	published	0	1	1	<h3><u>Introduction</u></h3><p><br></p><p>In order to achieve appropriate scrolling the following structure must be implemented</p><p><br></p><pre spellcheck="false">&lt;style&gt;\n\t.container{\n\t\theight:100%;\n\t\twidth:100%;\n\t\tposition:relative;\n\t\toverflow:hidden;\n\t}\n\t.contents{\n\t\theight:100%;\n\t\twidth:100%;\n\t\tposition:absolute;\n\t\toverflow:auto;\n\t}\n&lt;/style&gt;\n\n&lt;div class="container"&gt;\n\t&lt;div class="contents"&gt;\n\t\tThis would be scroll-able content.\n\t&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n</pre><p><br></p><p><span style="background-color: rgb(250, 204, 204);">Note: It is important to note that the container is not optional, it is a must and without the relative container there is no way for the contents to know the bounds required for scrolling</span></p>	\N
